  "id": "hadrami_dan_sawt",
  "name": "Dān and ṣawt ḥaḍramī (Hadrami song)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Hadramawt in eastern Yemen, spanning the dan, in which poets and singers develop verses over set melodies at evening gatherings, and the urban Hadrami sawt sung to the lute with drums. Singers such as Mohammed Jum'a Khan and Abu Bakr Salem Balfaqih, born in Tarim, carried it onto records and Gulf radio with ensembles of oud, violins and hand drums; the fiddle card stands for the violins and the hand drum card for the mirwas.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1940s dān and ṣawt ḥaḍramī, art Music, middle eastern classical branch. neutral third half flat, Arabic maqam, solo with instrumental accompaniment. oud, fiddle, hand drum source unspecified. am radio booth. Neumann U47, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp. tape 15ips hall reverb.",
